Project Title: International E-Commerce Website for a Premier Sri Lankan Gem Trader
1. Core Objective:
To design and develop a sophisticated, trustworthy, and visually stunning e-commerce website to showcase and sell high-quality, ethically sourced Sri Lankan gemstones to an international clientele. The primary goal is to build a strong online brand presence, establish trust with overseas buyers, and facilitate secure international transactions.

2. Target Audience:

International gem collectors and connoisseurs.

Luxury jewelry designers and brands worldwide.

Wholesale gem buyers.

Individuals seeking high-value gemstones for investment or personal use (e.g., engagement rings).

They value authenticity, quality certification, ethical sourcing, and a seamless, secure purchasing experience.

3. Key Website Pages & Features:

Homepage:

Hero Section: A full-screen, high-resolution video or image showcasing a signature gemstone (like a Ceylon Sapphire).

Value Proposition: Clear, concise headline like "The World's Finest Ceylon Sapphires, Direct from the Source."

Featured Gems: A curated gallery of new arrivals or best-selling stones.

Trust Signals: Prominently display logos of certifications (GIA, etc.) and memberships in gemological associations.

"Our Story" Teaser: A brief section linking to the full "About Us" page.

Gemstone Gallery / Shop:

Professional Listings: Each gem must have high-quality, well-lit photos and a 360-degree video on a clean background.

Detailed Information: For each stone, display: Gem Type, Carat Weight, Dimensions, Color, Cut, Clarity, Origin (Sri Lanka), Treatment, and Price (in USD).

Advanced Filtering & Sorting: Users MUST be able to filter by:

Gemstone Type (Sapphire, Ruby, Spinel, etc.)

Color

Carat Size Range

Price Range

Shape (Oval, Round, Cushion, etc.)

Certification: A clear icon indicating if a stone is certified, with the ability to view the certificate (PDF or image).

Product Detail Page:

An expanded view of the selected gem with a gallery of multiple images and the 360-degree video.

All specifications listed clearly.

A prominent "Add to Cart" or "Inquire" button.

Details on secure shipping, insurance, and return policy.

Our Story / About Us:

Tell the story of your business heritage and expertise in the Sri Lankan gem industry.

Include photos of the founders, the team, or the region.

Emphasize your connection to the local mining communities and your commitment to the craft.

Ethical Sourcing & The Journey of a Gem:

A dedicated page explaining your commitment to ethical, conflict-free sourcing.

Visually map out the process: from the mine, to cutting & polishing, to certification and final sale. This builds immense trust.

Education / Gemstone Guide:

Simple articles or infographics explaining the "4 Cs" (Cut, Color, Clarity, Carat).

A guide to the famous gemstones of Sri Lanka (especially Ceylon Sapphires).

Information on gemstone care.

Contact Page:

A simple contact form.

Business email address, phone number (with international dialing code).

Physical address in Sri Lanka with an embedded Google Map.

4. E-Commerce Functionality:

Secure Shopping Cart & Checkout: A clean, multi-step checkout process.

International Payment Gateway: Integration with a globally recognized provider like Stripe or PayPal to accept major credit cards.

Currency Switcher: Ability for users to view prices in major currencies (USD, EUR, GBP). USD should be the default.

Secure International Shipping: Integration with a reliable courier like FedEx or DHL, with options for insured shipping calculated at checkout.

5. Design & Aesthetics:

Look & Feel: Luxurious, elegant, clean, and professional. The design should feel as high-end as the products themselves.

Color Palette: A sophisticated palette of dark charcoal, deep navy blue, or black, accented with gold, silver, or white to make the gemstone colors pop.

Typography: A classic, elegant serif font (like Playfair Display or Garamond) for headings and a clean, readable sans-serif font (like Inter, Lato, or Montserrat) for body text.

Imagery: All photography and videography must be of the highest professional quality. This is non-negotiable.

6. Technical Requirements:

Fully Responsive: The website must look and function perfectly on desktops, tablets, and mobile phones.

SEO Optimized: Built with SEO best practices to rank for keywords like "buy Ceylon Sapphire online," "Sri Lankan gemstones," etc.

Fast Loading Speeds: Optimized images and code to ensure the site loads quickly worldwide.

SSL Certificate: Must be secured with HTTPS for user trust and data protection.

7. Content Management System (CMS):

User-Friendly Backend: The website must be built on a robust and intuitive CMS (like Shopify, or WordPress with WooCommerce) that allows for easy updates without technical knowledge.

Editable Content: The client must be able to easily:

Manage Inventory: Add, edit, delete, and mark gemstones as "sold." This includes updating all photos, videos, and specifications for each stone.

Update Pages: Edit the text and images on pages like "Our Story," "Ethical Sourcing," and the homepage.

Publish Articles: Add new posts to the "Education / Gemstone Guide" section.

Manage Orders: View and process incoming orders and customer inquiries.
